//! THE HANDLE a rule holds: an analysed file's view, plus one node
//! in it — the code in hand (P10), never a bare id, so a rule reads
//! it with no context parameter of its own. It never meets
//! `@std.meta.Code` in one file — that is a SPLICING value, built
//! at compile time from a template; this is a COMPILER-SIDE value, a
//! subject a `quote` PATTERN matches against. Slice 3 grows its
//! facts as properties here (`x.pure`, `x.type`, …).
use core.{At}

export type Code = { view: FileView, at: At }
